for the Arab world annual get-together  this year the leaders converged on  Algiers some representing countries in  turmoil others locked in a standoff over  power while many governed societies  struggling with dire social and economic  challenges  the conflict and crises are not just  within Arab countries the level of  representation was a sign of the uneasy  relationships among each other  Algeria says the Gathering is about  reunifying the Arab League but the  normalization of ties between Israel and  some Arab countries has further  polarized it and while leaders voiced  messages of support for Palestinian  rights and statehood the Gathering ended  without condemnation of Israel  dear brothers or Palestinian people are  facing racist policies with our  challenges we are expecting from you to  follow up to pursue your position by  activating the previous resolutions of  the Arab Summits  those taking part in the summit face the  challenge of crafting a final resolution  agreed by all a point of contention has  long been the role of non-arab actors  turkia and Iran the final communique  called for non-interference in Arab  Affairs and an end to the presence of  foreign forces but unlike some leaders  it didn't mention names  it wasn't the only divisive issue put  aside there was no agreement on Syria's  return to the Arab fold after more than  a decade of exclusion due to its brutal  Crackdown on Peaceful protests Syria's  reinstatement was something Russia had  been pushing for but it does appear to  have won another diplomatic battle the  Arab League didn't isolate Moscow and  remained neutral in the Ukraine conflict  in turn President Vladimir Putin told  the league Russia is ready to cooperate  with them to boost their security  the war in Ukraine has also affected  economies an increase in food and fuel  prices has worsened hunger in the Middle  East and North Africa and while Russia  may have reversed its decision to  suspend participation in the effort to  allow Ukraine to export grains it caused  concern we must do all we can to ensure  the continued success of the Black Sea  Green initiative to provide relief to  those in need geopolitical divides have  created a new reality in the Middle East  and North Africa where Russia and China  are gaining influence at the expense of  the U.S the final communique supported  the decision by OPEC plus to reduce oil  output which caused tensions between  Saudi Arabia and the United States but  many see it as the Revival of the old  Regional order where leaders use words  like Unity solidarity and Joint action  without offering solutions to the crises  Algiers
 

